mode: "100644"
text: "# Goals & KPIs 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile-ish. Re-verify benchmarks quarterly; the frameworks are stable.*\n\n## The cascade (the core structure)\n**Business goal → objective → KPI → supporting metrics.** Goals are broad and directional (\"build brand\nawareness\"); **objectives are specific, measurable, time-bound** (\"grow IG engagement 1.8% → 3.5% by Q4\n2026\"); **KPIs** are the metrics that prove the objective; supporting metrics are diagnostics. *\"An\nobjective without a number is a wish; without a deadline, a dream.\"* If a social goal doesn't **ladder\nup** to a business outcome, cut it.\n\n## North Star — one per channel\nPick **one North Star metric per channel**, tied to that channel's **win condition / role**:\n- **Awareness-first** (short-form video) → **reach / qualified impressions**.\n- **Consideration-first** (LinkedIn) → **CTR / link clicks** to an offer.\n- **Conversion-first** (retargeting, link-led) → **conversions / CPA**.\nCross-channel comparison only works when **each channel has its own win condition.** Add 1–2 supporting\nmetrics per North Star.\n\n## SMART (the litmus test)\n**S**pecific · **M**easurable · **A**chievable · **R**elevant · **T**ime-bound. \"Increase Reels\nengagement from 2.5% to 4% by end of Q2 2026\" is SMART; \"do better on Instagram\" is not. A good target\nalso **prevents gaming** — \"grow 10k → 11.5k **while holding 3%+ engagement rate**\" stops you buying fake\nfollowers to hit a number.\n\n## The KPI map = the funnel\nMirror how the business grows: **awareness → engagement → clicks → conversions → retention.** Reach =\ndistribution; clicks = intent; conversions = value. Anchor each objective to the right inflection point.\n\n## Hierarchy + the 3–5 rule\n**1 North Star → 3–5 strategic KPIs → operational KPIs → unlimited diagnostics.** Cap **objectives at\n3–5 per quarter** too (fewer = lack of ambition; more = fragmentation → prioritize ruthlessly). Too many\nKPIs dilute focus; too few hide problems.\n\n## Choosing a KPI (the criteria)\nStart from the **business objective** → identify **leading** (predict: reach, saves, engagement) vs\n**lagging** (confirm: revenue, conversions, churn) → **actionable** (you can take concrete steps) →\n**measurable** (data available consistently) → **correlated** (improving it drives results) →\n**controllable** (your team can actually influence it). Lead-gen must specify **quality** — doubling\nleads while halving conversion isn't progress.\n\n## Targets from benchmarks + action thresholds\nSet the number from a **benchmark**: your own **baseline** (extrapolate past performance) or comparable\naccounts — **achievable yet ambitious.** Make targets **trigger choices**: \"if reach holds but clicks\ndrop → change the hook/offer; if clicks rise but conversions fall → fix the landing page/tracking before\noptimizing content.\"\n\n## Review cadence\n**Weekly** (tactical metric check) · **monthly** (tactic performance) · **quarterly** (do the goals\nstill make sense?). **If a goal is missed, pivot tactics first — don't move the goalposts.** An **OKR**\nview helps tie social to revenue/pipeline/brand health for stakeholders. Setting targets is **this\nskill**; measuring against them is **analytics-and-reporting.**\n"
